## What still runs

Read-only watchers stay on, because a hold is not a blackout and K still needs to
see the account: `ax-rail-watchdog`, `ax-memory-guard`, `ax-risk-audit`,
`ax-roblox-live-state`, `ax-image-bank`, `ax-genart`, `ax-pc1-*` (PC1 tooling),
`ax-arena-*` / `ax-breachline-*` (Roblox). Rendering to local disk is also
allowed — K is rebuilding the production system, which needs renders.

## How to lift it

1. Delete this file: `git rm ops/PUBLISH-HOLD`.
2. Re-enable the rails K wants back:
   `PUT /actions/workflows/<id>/enable`.
3. Run `python3 ops/hold_gate.py` — it must print `open`.

Lifting the hold is K's call, not the agent's. Do not delete this file to make a
test or a run pass.
